---
# Enabled families (CLAUDE.md): bugprone, modernize, performance, cppcoreguidelines.
# Every exclusion below states why. Prefer fixing code or a narrow // NOLINT(check) with a
# reason over adding exclusions here.
Checks: >
  -*,
  bugprone-*,
  modernize-*,
  performance-*,
  cppcoreguidelines-*,
  -modernize-use-trailing-return-type,
  -cppcoreguidelines-owning-memory,
  -cppcoreguidelines-avoid-c-arrays,
  -modernize-avoid-c-arrays,
  -bugprone-easily-swappable-parameters,
  -cppcoreguidelines-avoid-magic-numbers,
  -cppcoreguidelines-pro-type-vararg,
  -cppcoreguidelines-macro-usage,
  -cppcoreguidelines-avoid-non-const-global-variables
# Exclusion reasons:
#  modernize-use-trailing-return-type
#      Style preference only; the project uses conventional leading return types.
#  cppcoreguidelines-owning-memory
#      Requires gsl::owner<>. Qt parent/child ownership (CLAUDE.md) hands raw pointers around
#      by design; the "no naked new/delete" rule is enforced by review instead.
#  cppcoreguidelines-avoid-c-arrays, modernize-avoid-c-arrays
#      main(int, char* argv[]) is the signature Qt (QApplication) and the C++ standard require.
#  bugprone-easily-swappable-parameters
#      Extremely noisy on ordinary APIs (e.g. two QString arguments); little real bug yield.
#  cppcoreguidelines-avoid-magic-numbers
#      Alias of readability-magic-numbers: flags every literal in UI geometry and in test data.
#  cppcoreguidelines-pro-type-vararg
#      Triggered by Qt (qDebug, QMessageLogger) and GoogleTest assertion macros.
#  cppcoreguidelines-macro-usage
#      Qt (Q_OBJECT, Q_ASSERT, ...) and GoogleTest (TEST, EXPECT_*) are macro based.
#  cppcoreguidelines-avoid-non-const-global-variables
#      GoogleTest's TEST() macro registers a global object for every test.
WarningsAsErrors: '*'
# Only report diagnostics for our own headers (not Qt, vcpkg or generated moc code).
HeaderFilterRegex: '.*[/\](src|tests)[/\].*'
FormatStyle: file
